flowchart TB

  v_emit["bufferCompleted.emit calls <br/>activate on connected slots <br/>in connection order. The <br/>emitter must ensure that <br/>pointers and references <br/>passed through the signal <br/>remain valid after emission."]
  v_activate["A member or functor <br/>activate packs the <br/>arguments and calls <br/>activatePack when there is <br/>an Object receiver; <br/>otherwise, it calls the <br/>function directly."]
  v_activatepack{"activatePack branches <br/>according to the connection <br/>type. Auto selects Direct <br/>on the same thread and <br/>Queued on different threads."}
  v_invokepack["For Direct, invokePack <br/>immediately calls the <br/>receiver function <br/>synchronously in the <br/>sender#39;s thread and returns <br/>after the receiver function <br/>returns. A nested call to <br/>the same function from a <br/>callback is forbidden <br/>unless separately allowed."]
  v_postmessage["For Queued, postMessage <br/>posts an InvokeMessage. The <br/>sender does not wait for <br/>the receiver function to <br/>finish; execution and <br/>completion of the receiver <br/>function are separate. The <br/>Object destructor may <br/>remove pending messages, so <br/>posting alone does not <br/>guarantee future delivery."]
  v_dispatch["dispatchMessages delivers <br/>posted messages matching <br/>the type and receiver <br/>filters in that thread. It <br/>can be called explicitly <br/>outside the normal event <br/>loop and recursively from a <br/>message handler in the same <br/>thread. Calling it from <br/>another thread has <br/>undefined behavior."]
  v_message["Object::message handles a <br/>consumed InvokeMessage in <br/>the object#39;s thread. This <br/>handling may start before <br/>or after emit returns or <br/>the internal update. An <br/>override must pass <br/>unhandled messages to the <br/>parent handler and must not <br/>retain a message reference <br/>after return."]
  v_completebuffer["After emit actually <br/>returns, <br/>Request::Private::<br/>completeBuffer removes <br/>buffer from pending#95; and <br/>clears the buffer#39;s request <br/>association, setting <br/>cancelled#95; if the buffer <br/>was cancelled. The request <br/>does not complete <br/>automatically when the last <br/>buffer completes, so the <br/>pipeline handler must call <br/>completeRequest#40;#41; <br/>explicitly."]
